# .deploy_protect
#
# Paths that must NEVER be deleted during a clean deploy.
#
# This file is committed to the repository and is the single source of
# truth for what survives a clean. It replaces the old hardcoded
# PROTECTED_PATHS set that used to live inside file_utils.py.
#
# HOW MATCHING WORKS
# ------------------
# One glob per line. A path is protected if EITHER:
#   - the full relative path matches a pattern
#     (e.g. "config/something/tokens.json")
#   - any single path component matches a pattern
#     (e.g. "tokens.json" matches at any depth)
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# A single trailing slash is stripped ("world/" behaves like "world").
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# A clean deploy wipes every file in the target directory that is not
# part of the source sync. That is correct for modpack-managed files
# and catastrophic for server-generated ones. Anything the server
# writes at runtime and that is not reproducible from the repo must be
# listed here, or it will be destroyed on the next clean deploy.
#
# WHEN TO ADD
# -----------
# When in doubt, add it. A false positive just means the deploy leaves
# the file in place instead of removing it — harmless. A false negative
# destroys data on the next clean deploy.

# ===========================================================================
# MINECRAFT SERVER RUNTIME
# ===========================================================================
# Standard files and directories the vanilla/Forge server writes on its
# own. None of these are in the git repo; all of them must survive.

server.properties
eula.txt
ops.json
whitelist.json
banned-ips.json
banned-players.json
usercache.json
usernamecache.json

# World data. Never touch.
world
world_nether
world_the_end

# Runtime logs and crash dumps.
logs
crash-reports

# Server launcher state written by the run scripts.
user_jvm_args.txt
.run-forge.env
.forge-manifest.json
.rcon-cli.env
.rcon-cli.yaml
run.sh
run.bat

# ===========================================================================
# PROXY / MULTI-INSTANCE
# ===========================================================================
# Files that tie each backend instance to the Velocity proxy, plus the
# proxy's own forwarding secret. All three are server-generated and
# must never be part of the git repo or the deployed source tree.
#
# Bare filenames are used (not full paths) because the clean phase
# matches against the path relative to each target instance. The
# velocity target sees "forwarding.secret" at its root; the survival
# and creative targets each see "config/proxy-compatible-forge.toml".
# One pattern covers both backend instances.

forwarding.secret
proxy-compatible-forge.toml

# ===========================================================================
# SERVER-AUTHORED MOD STATE
# ===========================================================================
# Mods that write their own config on first boot. These are the ones
# that bit us before — a clean deploy destroys them and the mod
# regenerates a fresh default, silently dropping any customized state.
#
# Add any mod that manages its own files under config/ or in the server
# root. Keep the list grouped by mod for legibility.

patchouli_books
schematics
defaultconfigs

# ===========================================================================
# JVM / FORGE / LAUNCHER
# ===========================================================================
# Forge's extracted libraries and binary tools. Deleting them forces a
# full re-extract on next boot. Not destructive, but slow.

bin
libraries

# ===========================================================================
# CACHE / EPHEMERAL
# ===========================================================================
# Safe to regenerate, but expensive or disruptive to force during a
# deploy. Protected as a matter of operational convenience.

local
.cache
.mixin.out

